        "body": "Gain 5, Work 2, Harm 4\nRaise: Functional\nCase: normal use - In a CI-test repository, a ready pull request reaches the default-branch health check. The query asks for `workflowRun.workflow.path`, but GitHub's [`Workflow` type](https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/actions#workflow) has no `path` field; the path is exposed on `WorkflowRun.file` instead. GitHub rejects the entire query during validation, so `red()` refuses every `forge merge` and also prevents the human `forge land` hand-off, even when the default branch is green. The test fixture at `tests/test_merge_waits_while_default_is_red.py:213` supplies the nonexistent field and therefore does not catch the failure.",
